1. PREAMBLE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Cluaiz Open Source License (COL) is designed to cultivate a high-performance,
collaborative ecosystem. By making our source code fully open, we empower every
developer, startup, researcher, and enterprise to build freely. This license protects
the platform from competing hosted clones while remaining free for all.

This is an OPEN SOURCE license. Anyone can use, modify, distribute, and self-host
the Licensed Software — whether for personal projects, commercial products, or
enterprise deployments — without any revenue threshold or mandatory commercial fee.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. DEFINITIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
"Licensed Software" means the source code, build scripts, configuration files, 
and documentation of the Cluaiz ecosystem made available under this License.

"Enterprise" means any corporate entity, business, or organization that operates
a Competing SaaS / Hosted Service using the Licensed Software.

"Contributor" means any individual or corporate entity that has authored and 
had an accepted merged contribution in the official upstream repository of the 
Licensed Software.

"Competing SaaS / Hosted Service" means any service that provides the core 
functional features of the Licensed Software as a hosted platform, managed API, 
managed container, or cloud offering in direct commercial competition with the 
official cloud services or commercial API endpoints hosted by Cluaiz.

